Route Tables in DevOps
 
Your cloud needs directions. That’s what route tables do.
 
Think of them as maps for your EC2 traffic — guiding it in or out.
 
No route = no connection
Even if your instance is up and running, it can’t reach the outside world without the right route.
 
Example: Want your EC2 to download updates? It needs a route to send traffic through the Internet Gateway. No path? No internet.
